---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { t } from "../i18n";

const locale = "en";
const title = `${t("site.name", locale)} · The story`;
const description =
  "From a 610-metre grass strip in 1978 and a £85 ticket on Christmas Eve 1985 to the world's most scenic runway and Ireland's first ACA Level 4 carbon-accredited airport. The story of CFN.";

// Each chapter is data-driven so the layout repeats consistently
// and adding photos later is a single insert per chapter. `lead`
// is the opening paragraph (bigger, lighter); `body` is the array
// of standard paragraphs that follow.
const chapters = [
  {
    year: "1978",
    range: "Before the airport",
    title: "A grass strip on the dunes.",
    lead:
      "In the mid-1970s the IDA was trying to keep the west of Ireland alive with industrial estates. The one at Annagry needed an air link. In March 1978, on a sandbar between the Atlantic and Mount Errigal, a 610-metre grass runway opened.",
    body: [
      "For seven years no scheduled flight took off from it. A handful of private aircraft, the odd connection to Derry, and a runway that disappeared under blown sand every winter.",
      "By the mid-1980s the grass was replaced with a hard surface and a temporary prefab terminal went up. Donegal had an aerodrome. It just didn't have an airline yet.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "24.12.1985",
    range: "Christmas Eve",
    title: "A lawyer, an Islander, and an eighty-five-pound ticket.",
    lead:
      "On Christmas Eve 1985 Frank Cannon — a Glasgow solicitor with a father from Ardara and a mother from Ranafast — flew the first commercial service himself. A nine-seat Britten-Norman Islander, fifty-five minutes to Glasgow, £85 one way.",
    body: [
      "The idea had been hatched over dinner with Danny \"Minnie\" O'Brien, a restaurateur in Annagry. The airline was Malinair. By the summer of 1986 it was running ten rotations a day from six in the morning, the Islanders had been replaced by Dorniers, and Edinburgh and Manchester were on the timetable. By 1987 Malinair was bankrupt and Air Ecosse stepped in for a few weeks. The dream was over. The aerodrome had become an airport.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "1988 – 1997",
    range: "The Loganair years",
    title: "Loganair returns. The runway grows. Ryanair tries Luton.",
    lead:
      "In 1988 Loganair came back to Glasgow and stayed for a decade. The runway was extended at the end of the eighties to 1,450 metres so it could take bigger turboprops, and again in 1992–93 to 1,500 metres. In 1990 Ryanair launched a service to London Luton.",
    body: [
      "And in the winter of 1994 the storms ran for weeks. The ferry to Tory Island couldn't sail. The Irish Air Corps moved their helicopters to Carrickfinn and ran supplies — bread, post, prescriptions, schoolchildren — out to the island until the sea calmed down. The pattern stuck. For decades after, the helicopter to Tory would route through CFN whenever the weather closed in on Magheroarty.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "·",
    range: "Of the people who built it",
    title: "Anthony Gillespie.",
    lead:
      "Every small airport has a handful of names without whom it would never have lasted. At Donegal, Anthony Gillespie is one of them.",
    body: [
      "An early shareholder of the project, a promoter, and the public face of the airport through much of its formative period — his work runs from the consolidation of the commercial service in the late eighties through the establishment of the Dublin PSO in the nineties. The people who were here in those years remember his role well beyond what the public record bothered to write down.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "1996 – 2008",
    range: "The PSO years",
    title: "Dublin every day. A team that stayed.",
    lead:
      "In August 1996 the Donegal–Dublin PSO was awarded for the first time, one of the very first PSO routes in Ireland. Ireland Airways flew it, then Aer Arann from 1998, then Euroceltic, then Aer Arann again. By 2008 the airport was carrying 65,539 passengers — the all-time record.",
    body: [
      "Anne Bonner had been at the airport since the very beginning, working in customer services. In 2002 she was named Managing Director, a role she would hold for two decades.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "2001 – 2010",
    range: "Helicopters out west",
    title: "The Atlantic margin runs on Donegal fuel.",
    lead:
      "For a stretch of about a decade Donegal was something else entirely: the closest paved runway with refuelling to the offshore oil and gas exploration in the Atlantic margin. Bristow Helicopters ran the shuttle.",
    body: [
      "Two basins drove the traffic. The Slyne-Erris Trough off Mayo, where the Corrib gas field had been discovered in 1996, and the deeper Rockall Trough where in 2002 Enterprise (about to be absorbed by Shell) drilled the Dooish well — 125 kilometres northwest of Donegal, 1,478 metres of water under the rig. Both campaigns needed crews changed every couple of weeks and a fuel stop that wasn't four hundred miles away.",
      "Passenger numbers at CFN went from 11,566 in 2000 to 42,675 in 2004. The Irish economy doesn't account for that jump on its own. The helicopters do.",
      "After the oil-price crash of 2014, the appraisal flights tapered. Corrib went into onshore production in 2015. In 2017 the Druid/Drombeg exploration well off Cork came up dry, and west-of-Ireland exploration quietly closed for the foreseeable future. The hangar at CFN went back to scheduled traffic and the occasional Air Corps movement.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "2018 · 2019 · 2020",
    range: "Three years in a row",
    title: "The world's most scenic runway.",
    lead:
      "PrivateFly, the global private-jet broker, asks pilots and travellers every year to name the airport with the best approach in the world. In April 2018 Donegal went straight to number one. Adam Twidell, the CEO of PrivateFly, called it \"extraordinarily beautiful and deservedly in the top spot.\"",
    body: [
      "It came first again in 2019. And in 2020. Three years in a row — a result no other airport on the list has ever managed.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "2025",
    range: "Today",
    title: "Greener than Dublin.",
    lead:
      "In January 2025 Donegal became the first airport on the island of Ireland to reach Airport Carbon Accreditation Level 4 \"Transformation\" — ahead of Dublin, Cork and Shannon.",
    body: [
      "Solar on the hangar roof. MVHR through the terminal. LED everything. Four 22-kilowatt EV chargers in the car park. The road to a seventy-per-cent reduction in scope-1 and scope-2 emissions by 2030, and Net Zero by 2050.",
      "Emerald Airlines flies Dublin twice a day under the Aer Lingus Regional brand. Loganair is year-round to Glasgow. The airport carried 50,530 passengers in 2024, up twenty-one per cent.",
    ],
  },
];

// Airlines that have served CFN, in order of arrival. Year column
// kept terse — the editorial paragraphs above carry the story.
const airlines = [
  { name: "Malinair", route: "Glasgow / Manchester / Edinburgh", years: "1985 – 1987" },
  { name: "Air Ecosse", route: "Glasgow", years: "1987" },
  { name: "Loganair", route: "Glasgow", years: "1988 – 1997" },
  { name: "Ryanair", route: "London Luton", years: "from 1990" },
  { name: "Macair", route: "—", years: "1995" },
  { name: "Gill Airways", route: "Glasgow Prestwick", years: "1996 –" },
  { name: "Ireland Airways", route: "Dublin PSO", years: "1996 – 1998" },
  { name: "Bright Air", route: "Glasgow", years: "1997/98 –" },
  { name: "Aer Arann", route: "Dublin · Cork · Glasgow Intl.", years: "1998 – 2015" },
  { name: "Euroceltic", route: "Dublin PSO", years: "2001 – 2003" },
  { name: "Loganair / Flybe", route: "Dublin", years: "2012 – 2015" },
  { name: "Stobart Air (Aer Lingus Regional)", route: "Dublin PSO", years: "2015 – 2021" },
  { name: "Amapola Flyg", route: "Dublin PSO (interim)", years: "2021 – 2022" },
  { name: "Emerald Airlines (Aer Lingus Regional)", route: "Dublin PSO · 2× daily", years: "2022 – today" },
  { name: "Loganair (relaunch)", route: "Glasgow · year-round", years: "2023 – today" },
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  {/* ---------- HERO — text only. Photo will replace the cream
       backdrop once we choose one. ---------- */}
  <section
    class="relative isolate flex min-h-[78vh] w-full items-end border-b border-line bg-surface-lo/40"
  >
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-6 pb-20 pt-44 sm:pb-32">
      <p
        data-animate="fade-up"
        class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.32em] text-atlantic"
      >
        About · An scéal
      </p>
      <h1
        data-split
        data-split-delay="0.1"
        class="mt-8 max-w-5xl font-display text-[clamp(2.75rem,7vw,7.5rem)] font-light leading-[0.95] text-ink"
      >
        Forty years on the beach.
      </h1>
      <p
        data-animate="fade-up"
        data-animate-delay="0.35"
        class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-mute sm:text-lg"
      >
        From a 610-metre grass strip in 1978 and a Christmas-Eve
        ticket in 1985 to the world's most scenic runway and
        Ireland's greenest airport. The story of CFN — told in
        pieces.
      </p>

      <div
        data-animate="fade-up"
        data-animate-delay="0.5"
        class="mt-14 flex items-center gap-3 text-mute"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <span class="scroll-hint font-mono text-[0.65rem] uppercase tracking-[0.24em]">
          Scroll
        </span>
        <span class="scroll-hint text-base">↓</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ---------- TIMELINE ---------- */}
  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-24 sm:py-32">
      <ol class="space-y-24 sm:space-y-32">
        {
          chapters.map((c, i) => (
            <li class="relative">
              {/* Decorative chapter index — small, mono, far left */}
              <p class="absolute -left-2 top-1 hidden font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-mute sm:block sm:-left-20">
                {`0${i + 1}`.slice(-2)}
              </p>

              <p
                data-animate="fade-up"
                class="font-mono text-[0.72rem] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-sand"
              >
                <span>{c.range}</span>
                {c.year !== "·" && (
                  <span class="ml-3 text-atlantic">{c.year}</span>
                )}
              </p>

              <h2
                data-split
                class="mt-5 font-display text-[clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3.8rem)] font-light leading-[1.02] text-ink"
              >
                {c.title}
              </h2>

              <p
                data-animate="fade-up"
                data-animate-delay="0.15"
                class="mt-7 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-ink sm:text-[1.15rem]"
              >
                {c.lead}
              </p>

              {c.body.map((para, j) => (
                <p
                  data-animate="fade-up"
                  data-animate-delay={`${0.2 + (j + 1) * 0.05}`}
                  class="mt-5 text-base leading-[1.75] text-mute"
                >
                  {para}
                </p>
              ))}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ---------- AIRLINES TABLE ---------- */}
  <section class="border-t border-line bg-surface-lo/60">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-24">
      <p
        data-animate="fade-up"
        class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-atlantic"
      >
        Operators
      </p>
      <h2
        data-split
        class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-display text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,3.4rem)] font-light leading-[1.04]"
      >
        Every airline that has flown to Donegal.
      </h2>

      <div data-animate="fade-up" class="mt-12 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-y border-line text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-mute">
              <th class="py-3 pr-6 font-medium">Airline</th>
              <th class="py-3 pr-6 font-medium">Route</th>
              <th class="py-3 font-medium">Years</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="font-mono text-sm">
            {
              airlines.map((a) => (
                <tr class="border-b border-line/60">
                  <td class="py-4 pr-6 text-ink">{a.name}</td>
                  <td class="py-4 pr-6 text-mute">{a.route}</td>
                  <td class="py-4 tabular-nums text-mute">{a.years}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ---------- CHARACTERS — text only, no photos yet ---------- */}
  <section class="border-t border-line">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-24">
      <p
        data-animate="fade-up"
        class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-atlantic"
      >
        The people behind it
      </p>
      <h2
        data-split
        class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-display text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,3.4rem)] font-light leading-[1.04]"
      >
        Four names without which none of this happens.
      </h2>

      <ul class="mt-14 grid gap-12 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {
          [
            {
              name: "Frank Cannon",
              role: "Founder of Malinair",
              years: "1985 – 1987",
              body: "Glasgow solicitor, private pilot. Father from Ardara, mother from Ranafast. Flew the first commercial service from Donegal himself, Christmas Eve 1985.",
            },
            {
              name: 'Daniel "Minnie" O\'Brien',
              role: "The dinner that started it",
              years: "1985",
              body: "Restaurateur in Annagry. The conversation with him is what convinced Cannon the place needed — and could sustain — a way out.",
            },
            {
              name: "Anthony Gillespie",
              role: "Shareholder · promoter · public face",
              years: "Late 1980s onwards",
              body: "An early shareholder and one of the most active promoters of the airport through the late eighties and the nineties. The people who were there in those years remember his role well beyond what the public record bothered to write down.",
            },
            {
              name: "Anne Bonner",
              role: "Managing Director",
              years: "2002 – ~2023",
              body: "Joined in customer services on day one. Twenty years as Managing Director took the airport through the years that built it: the PSO, the helicopters, the awards.",
            },
          ].map((p, i) => (
            <li
              data-animate="fade-up"
              data-animate-delay={`${0.05 + i * 0.05}`}
              class="border-t border-line pt-6"
            >
              <p class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-sand">
                {p.years}
              </p>
              <p class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl text-ink sm:text-3xl">
                {p.name}
              </p>
              <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-mute">
                {p.role}
              </p>
              <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-[1.7] text-mute">{p.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ---------- CTA CLOSER ---------- */}
  <section class="border-t border-line bg-surface-lo/40">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-32 text-center">
      <p
        data-animate="fade-up"
        class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-atlantic"
      >
        Come and see
      </p>
      <h2
        data-split
        class="mt-4 font-display text-[clamp(2rem,5vw,4.8rem)] font-light leading-[1]"
      >
        The runway is on a beach.<br />Bring a camera.
      </h2>
      <div
        data-animate="fade-up"
        data-animate-delay="0.3"
        class="mt-14 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-6"
      >
        <a
          href="/flights"
          class="border-b border-ink/60 pb-1 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-ink transition-colors hover:border-sand hover:text-sand"
        >
          Today's flights →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/discover"
          class="border-b border-transparent pb-1 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-mute transition-colors hover:border-sand hover:text-sand"
        >
          Discover Donegal →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
